        "title" : null,
        "hasTitle" : false,
        "message" : [
          "%md",
          "",
          "This query treats the fraud data as a graph. In the MATCH pattern, (seed IS entity) is the starting account, -[e IS related_to]->{1,2} means follow one or two relationship hops, and (reached IS entity) is every entity reached from that starting point.",
          "",
          "The WHERE clause anchors the search on ACCT-8841, and the COLUMNS clause returns graph properties in a normal SQL result table.",
          "",
          "This is much easier than writing the same logic with ordinary joins. Without SQL/PGQ graph pattern matching, you would need separate self-joins for one-hop and two-hop paths, extra union logic for each relationship depth, and more code every time investigators want to follow another type of relationship.",
          "",
          "The graph pattern says the investigation in plain terms: start with this account, follow the relationships, and show what is connected."
        ],
        "selectedVisualization" : "html",
        "visualizationConfig" : null,
        "hideCode" : true,
        "hideResult" : false,
        "hideGutter" : true,
        "hideVizConfig" : false,
        "hideInIFrame" : false,
        "enabled" : true,
        "forms" : "[]",
        "result" : {
          "startTime" : 1785963514722,
          "endTime" : 1785963514772,
          "interpreter" : "md",
          "taskStatus" : "SUCCESS",
          "status" : "SUCCESS",
          "results" : [
            {
              "message" : "<p>This query treats the fraud data as a graph. In the MATCH pattern, (seed IS entity) is the starting account, -[e IS related_to]-&gt;{1,2} means follow one or two relationship hops, and (reached IS entity) is every entity reached from that starting point.</p>\n<p>The WHERE clause anchors the search on ACCT-8841, and the COLUMNS clause returns graph properties in a normal SQL result table.</p>\n<p>This is much easier than writing the same logic with ordinary joins. Without SQL/PGQ graph pattern matching, you would need separate self-joins for one-hop and two-hop paths, extra union logic for each relationship depth, and more code every time investigators want to follow another type of relationship.</p>\n<p>The graph pattern says the investigation in plain terms: start with this account, follow the relationships, and show what is connected.</p>\n",
              "type" : "HTML"
            }
          ],
          "forms" : "[]"
        },
        "relations" : [ ],
        "dynamicFormParams" : "{}"
      },
